  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Don Davis built his original fortune in Texas food distribution before selling that business in the 1990s. He then established Great Texas Foods, opening the Brazos Cattle Company and Café Del Rio concepts and acquiring seafood and Italian restaurants. The group gave him a durable operating base in food service while he pursued other investments from Texas and Florida.\n\nDavis entered shipbuilding when Sovereign failed while constructing a vessel for him in British Columbia. Rather than abandon the project, he funded its completion, bought the yard’s assets and launched Richmond Yachts in 2004. As majority owner, president and chief executive, he retained much of the workforce and adopted a speculative semi-custom production model. The yard produced seven large composite motor vessels before operations ended in 2015.",
    "html": "<p>Don Davis built his original fortune in Texas food distribution before selling that business in the 1990s. He then established Great Texas Foods, opening the Brazos Cattle Company and Café Del Rio concepts and acquiring seafood and Italian restaurants. The group gave him a durable operating base in food service while he pursued other investments from Texas and Florida.</p>\r\n<p>Davis entered shipbuilding when Sovereign failed while constructing a vessel for him in British Columbia. Rather than abandon the project, he funded its completion, bought the yard’s assets and launched Richmond Yachts in 2004. As majority owner, president and chief executive, he retained much of the workforce and adopted a speculative semi-custom production model. The yard produced seven large composite motor vessels before operations ended in 2015.</p>\r\n",
